{
  "title": "Serialize UI dependency installation across concurrent make targets",
  "description": "Running make lint and make test concurrently in a fresh worktree makes both invoke npm ci through the UI_DEPS_MARKER rule. \
During placeholder-image filtering validation, one installation exited 239 and the other left client generation unable to locate TypeScript (npx canceled due to missing tsc). \
The generate-clients script has a lock, but the prerequisite UI install does not. \
Serialize installation across make processes so concurrent validation cannot corrupt node_modules. \
Reinstalling with make -W ramekin-ui/package-lock.json ui-deps and then regenerating clients sequentially repairs the setup. \
This is build tooling shared by web and generated client validation; no client behavior change is needed.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "web",
  ],
